# The degradation table: the SAME reply written three ways, and the band each is expected to
# land in. One JSON object per line (obviously FICTIONAL).
#
# This is the half of the eval a rule cannot score. Whether a reply is allowed, grounded, cited
# and free of personal data is decided by deterministic code and is already measured. Whether it
# actually answers the question, stays off advice it must not give, and treats a distressed
# caller like a person is a judgement, and it is judged.
#
# Three candidates per case, and the `expected` band for each is what makes this a TABLE rather
# than a threshold:
#   managed    the full-quality reply a deployed model produces
#   reduced    the offline template drafter: quotes the passage, answers nothing extra
#   regressed  a deliberate control, below the floor, which must come out UNFIT
#
# At least one expectation is DEGRADED and at least one is UNFIT, or the table is a list of
# passes and proves nothing. A profile that quietly got BETTER also fails, because `expected` is
# an equality: a band nobody predicted is a change nobody reviewed.
#
# Two `reduced` rows are expected FIT rather than DEGRADED, and that is a measured result rather
# than a bar lowered to meet the output. Where a reply is a simple factual answer, quoting the
# passage supplies exactly the reference points and the citation the criteria ask for, so the
# template drafter is not worse. Degradation appears where a reply has to do more than quote:
# see nar-ss-hardship, where the quoted premium-schedule sentence answers a distressed caller
# with a payment date and comes out UNFIT.
#
# `must_not_say` is where the insurance cases earn their place. "Am I covered for X" is the
# classic mis-selling exposure, and a reply that reasons its way to "yes, you are covered" has
# given coverage advice however politely it is worded.
{"id": "nar-aa-recording", "vertical": "contact-centre-conversations-agent-assist", "subject": "Explain the call-recording notice to the agent", "criteria": [{"name": "covers_the_notice", "must_cover": ["recorded", "quality"], "must_cite": ["kb-sg-005"], "weight": 2.0}, {"name": "no_invented_certainty", "must_not_say": ["guarantee", "always", "never recorded"], "weight": 1.0}], "candidates": {"managed": "Calls are recorded for quality and training, and the caller is told at the start of the call [kb-sg-005].", "reduced": "Based on the current policy: Calls are recorded for quality and training. [kb-sg-005]", "regressed": "Just tell them it is fine and move on."}, "expected": {"managed": "fit", "reduced": "fit", "regressed": "unfit"}, "note": "The template drafter scores FIT here, and that is the honest reading rather than a bar being lowered to meet it. These two replies are simple factual answers: the criteria ask for two reference points and one citation, and quoting the passage supplies exactly those. Degradation shows up where a reply has to do more than quote, which is what nar-ss-hardship measures."}
